{% extends "_report_base.html.j2" %}

{# Shares the subject index's stylesheet and its table rules: the two are the same kind of
   page, one over a subject's runs and one over a dyad's windows, and only what differs
   is here. #}
{% block css %}
.subtitle { color: #7f8c8d; font-size: 0.85rem; }
.page-header {
  display: block;
  border-bottom: 2px solid #2980b9; padding-bottom: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
}
th, td { padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem; white-space: nowrap; }
tbody tr:hover { background: #f8fafc; }
td a { color: #2980b9; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
td a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.muted { color: #95a5a6; }
.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
td.flag { background: #fdf0e3; font-weight: 600; color: #b9591a; }
td.flag::after { content: " *"; color: #e08b3f; }
/* the whole-run row is the average over every condition below it, so it reads as a
   heading for them rather than as one more window */
tr.whole td { background: #f4f6f8; font-weight: 600; }
tr.whole td.num { font-weight: 600; }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
{% endblock %}

{% block header %}
<div class="page-header">
  <h1>{{ page_heading }}</h1>
  <span class="subtitle">
    {{ rows | length }} window{{ "s" if rows | length != 1 }} over
    {{ n_tasks }} task{{ "s" if n_tasks != 1 }}
    {%- if subject_ids %} &bull; {{ subject_ids | join(" &times; ") }}{% endif %}
    {%- if band %} &bull; band {{ band }}{% endif %}
    &bull; v{{ versions.get('fnirs-pipe', 'unknown') }} &bull; {{ run_date }}
  </span>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<h2>Windows</h2>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Window</th>
      {% if has_pairs %}<th>Pair</th>{% endif %}
      <th>Task</th>
      <th>Span</th>
      {% for c in chroma %}<th>WTC {{ chroma_labels[c] }}</th>{% endfor %}
      {% for c in chroma %}<th>inside COI {{ chroma_labels[c] }}</th>{% endfor %}
      {% for c in chroma %}<th>ISC {{ chroma_labels[c] }}</th>{% endfor %}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in rows %}
    <tr{% if row.condition is none %} class="whole"{% endif %}>
      <td>
        {% if row.href %}
          <a href="{{ row.href }}">{{ row.condition or "whole run" }}</a>
        {% else %}
          {{ row.condition or "whole run" }} <span class="muted">(no page)</span>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      {% if has_pairs %}<td>{{ row.pair or "" }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td>{{ row.task }}</td>
      <td class="num">{% if row.window %}{{ row.window }}{% else %}<span class="muted">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
      {% for c in chroma %}
      <td class="num{% if row.flagged.get(c) %} flag{% endif %}">
        {%- if c in row.coherence %}{{ "%.3f"|format(row.coherence[c]) }}
        {%- else %}<span class="muted">n/a</span>{% endif -%}
      </td>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for c in chroma %}
      <td class="num">
        {%- if c in row.valid_frac %}{{ "%.0f%%"|format(row.valid_frac[c] * 100) }}
        {%- else %}<span class="muted">n/a</span>{% endif -%}
      </td>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for c in chroma %}
      <td class="num">
        {%- if c in row.isc %}{{ "%+.3f"|format(row.isc[c]) }}
        {%- else %}<span class="muted">&mdash;</span>{% endif -%}
      </td>
      {% endfor %}
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p class="subtitle" style="margin-top:0.6rem;">
  Coherence is the mean over the homologous channel pairs, the band mean each window's own
  table holds; a crossed run's off-diagonal pairings are in the tables and on each page, not
  averaged into this column. <b>inside COI</b> is the share of band cells that fell inside
  the cone of influence, so a window near either end of the recording keeps fewer.
  <b>ISC</b> is the mean same-channel inter-brain correlation. Unlike the coherence it is
  cut from the recording rather than read out of a whole-record transform, and both are
  right: a correlation has no frequency axis and nothing in it filters, so a window carries
  no edge the record would not have had, while a wavelet transform of a cut window would
  have two edges and a cone of its own. Each window is z-scored inside itself, the
  correlation over a stretch being against that stretch's mean. Open a window for its
  coherence maps, its matrices and the phase arrows.
  {% if rows | length >= 4 %}
  A marked cell sits more than {{ outlier_z }} median absolute deviations from this dyad's
  other windows on that chromophore. It says the window differs from its neighbours, not
  that it failed.
  {% endif %}
</p>

<p class="subtitle">
  The whole-run row averages across every condition under it, so for a block design it is a
  summary and not a result. Rows marked as windows were read out of the whole-run wavelet
  transform, which is what keeps a short condition from being inflated by edges of its own;
  a tree whose conditions were cropped to separate files before the analysis shows them as
  separate tasks instead, each with a whole-run row of its own.
</p>

{% endblock %}
